1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:11,225
Cooks prepare ingredients before cooking: wash, cut, measure. Data needs the same: clean it, fill or drop missing values, and fix typos.

2
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:17,845
Scale numbers so a salary in millions does not drown out an age in tens.

3
00:00:19,550 --> 00:00:26,425
Some rows have blanks. You can drop them, or fill them with a sensible value like the median.

4
00:00:27,130 --> 00:00:34,180
But note how many you filled. If half the column is blank, the column may not be useful at all.

5
00:00:34,880 --> 00:00:41,305
Categories like city need turning into numbers before most models can use them.

6
00:00:43,000 --> 00:00:49,550
Keep some data hidden for the final test, like exam questions the students never saw.

7
00:00:50,250 --> 00:00:56,925
If the model sees the test data while learning, its score is a lie. Split first, always.

